# Poultry Intelligence Hub — product rules

Follow the full instructions in `AGENTS.md` at the repository root. Summary:

## Product
Mobile-first app for Indian broiler farmers. Turn farm data into clear decisions within 5–10 seconds of opening the app. Show numbers with meaning (e.g. "4.2% above expected"), not raw statistics. No decorative charts, gradients, glass effects, or fake-futuristic AI visuals.

## Hard rules
1. No hard-coded colors, sizes, or font sizes — theme tokens only.
2. No hard-coded user-facing text — everything through i18n (`t('key')`).
3. Layouts must grow; do not truncate important labels.
4. Touch targets ≥ 48px; primary actions ≥ 56px.
5. Status is never color alone — always icon + word (Normal / Watch / Act).
6. Offline first — local SQLite then sync queue; every record shows sync state.
7. Money is integer **paise**, formatted for display only (Indian grouping).
8. Calculations are deterministic code; the LLM may only explain results.
9. Plain language; explain FCR in one line the first time it appears.
10. Accessibility: labels on interactive elements; WCAG AA contrast.

## Structure
- `apps/web/` — Vite React browser UI
- `apps/api/` — FastAPI backend
- `apps/mobile/` — Expo app
- `apps/worker/` — Celery worker
- `supabase/` — Postgres migrations + RLS
- `design/` — design tokens
- `docs/` — organized documentation (see `docs/README.md`)

## Working style
Small reviewable changes. Test pure calculation functions. Ask when requirements conflict with these rules. Never invent farm data in production code.
